    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD070408",
      "title": "Optimization of Protein UFMylation Modification Method and Its Application in Substrate Identification in Human Cells",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "In this study, we generated the UFSP1KO/UFSP2KO HEK293T cell line and validated it as the most suitable cellular model for the screening, identification, and confirmation of UFMylated substrate proteins. Furthermore, exogenous expression of the E3 ligase components UFL1 and DDRGK1 significantly enhances protein UFMylation levels, enabling the large-scale enrichment of UFMylated substrates.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Human HEK293T cells were purchased from the American Type Culture Collection (ATCC) and cultured in DMEM (01-055-1A, Biological Industries), supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (FBS) (FSP500, ExCell Bio) and 1% penicillin-streptomycin (15140-122, Gibco). All cell lines were O2 incubator (Thermo Fisher Scientific). Transfection of constructs was 263 performed using Lipofectamine 3000 (Invitrogen) following the manufacturer's instructions.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "For LC-MS/MS analysis, the resulting peptides were desalted using C18 ZipTips (ZTC18S096, 341 Merck Millipore) following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. After adding iRT peptides, samples were analyzed by LC-MS/MS on an Orbitrap Astral Mass Spectrometer coupled to a nanoflow Vanquish Neo HPLC system (Thermo Fisher Scientific). Data were acquired in data-independent acquisition (DIA) mode. The analysis was performed in positive ion mode, with a full MS1 scan range of 380-980 345 \u00a0 m/z. MS1 spectra were acquired at a resolution of 240,000 (at 200 m/z) with a normalized Automatic Gain Control (AGC) target of 500% and a maximum injection time of 5 ms. For DIA of MS2 spectra, a method with 300 variable windows and an isolation width of 2 m/z was employed. MS2 scans were conducted using Higher-energy Collisional Dissociation (HCD) with a collision energy of 25 eV, a normalized AGC target of 300%, and a maximum injection time of 3 ms. LC-MS/MS experiments were performed by Micrometer Biotech Company (Hangzhou, China). A list of candidate protein \u00a0peptides is provided in the supplementary data.  For data processing, the resulting LC-MS/MS data were analyzed with Spectronaut software, and tandem mass spectra were searched against the UniProt-Human database. The software parameters were set as follows: enzyme was set to trypsin, maximum missed cleavages were set to 2, fixed modification was Carbamidomethyl (C), dynamic modifications included Oxidation (M), Acetyl (Protein N-term), and UFMylation (K). The False Discovery Rate (FDR) was set to < 1%.",
      "projectTags": [],
